@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_ActionsPopover}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Accessibility}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Actions_Popover @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Actions_Popover @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility . . . In Progress . . .</h1>

<p>
    The Actions Popover was built using the HTML Popover API so has the escape key and light dismiss functionality is handled by the browsers. Additionally
    a focus out handler was added so on tabbing out of the actions popover it would also close, in order to prevent it obscuring items beneath it especially 
    when used a row actions popover in a data table.
</p>

<h2 id="history-dialog-keyboard">Keyboard interaction</h2>
<p>
    The following keys are used for both the alerts button and the announcement history dialog.
</p>
<h2 id="actions-popover-keyboard">Actions popover keys</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="actions-popover-keyboard">
    <li><kbd>Enter or Space</kbd> - when focus is on the actions popover triggering button opens or closes the popover.</li>
    <li><kbd>Escape</kbd> - closes the popover and returns the focus to the triggering button that opened the popover.</li>
    <li><kbd>Tab</kbd> - moves focus to the next focusable item in the tab sequence (and closes the popover if that item is not part of the actions popover).</li>
    <li><kbd>Tab + Shift</kbd> - moves focus to the previous focusable item in the tab sequence.</li>
    <li><kbd>Enter or Space</kbd> - activates the focused button.</li>
    <li><kbd>Enter</kbd> - activates the focused link.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    <strong>Note:</strong> Clicking outside of the popover with the mouse closes the dialog.
</p>


<h2 id="device-testing">Accessibility device testing</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="device-testing">
    <li>JAWS, Narrator and NVDA on Windows were each paired with every one of the following browsers: Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge and Mozilla Firefox.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on macOS was paired with Apple's Safari.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on iPhone was paired with mobile Safari.</li>
    <li>Talkback on Android was paired with mobile Google Chrome.</li>
    <li>Voice access on Windows 11</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> Testing was performed with the latest browser and assistive technologies versions that were available at the time of testing (see release history on the installation page for approximate testing dates)
</p>


